  "title": "reassemble: Don't memcmp past the allocated buffer (datalen)",
  "description": "It's possible to have mutiple fragments added to a reassembly\nthat are past the end of the reassembly (given by a known datalen)\nthat overlap. We don't check those for overlap conflict, we only\ncheck against the buffer, which is pre-allocated to the known\ndatalen.\n\nFix #21408",
